# Salesforce metadata files that are corrupted by `xmlWhitespaceSensitivity: ignore`.
# Two failure modes:
#
#  1. External Service Registration files embed an escaped JSON payload inside
#     the <schema> element. Prettier inserts whitespace around the &quot;
#     entities that delimit the JSON strings, corrupting the schema and making
#     the file undeployable ("The schema is not supported or we could not
#     identify the schema type from your API spec").
#
#  2. Permission Set files include <externalCredentialPrincipal> cross-reference
#     ids (e.g. `mvpbo3__googleMapsMCP-googleApiKey`) that must be the exact
#     text content of the element. Prettier wraps long element contents to a
#     new line, which the Metadata API then sees as
#     "\n      mvpbo3__googleMapsMCP-googleApiKey\n    " and rejects with
#     "invalid cross reference id". The same file's <description> text also
#     gets whitespace inserted around &apos; entities.
#
# Keep these files out of prettier's reach. Add additional metadata-type
# patterns here if you discover similar formatting issues elsewhere.
**/externalServiceRegistrations/*.externalServiceRegistration-meta.xml
**/permissionsets/*.permissionset-meta.xml